<title>AUSTRALIA: Newcrest eyes A$5-$6 mln Telfer savings.</title>
<headline>Newcrest eyes A$5-$6 mln Telfer savings.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Newcrest Mining Ltd said on Tuesday it hopes to save between A$6 million and A$7 million annually from a restructuring of its Telfer gold mine mine in Western Australia.</p>
<p>Newcrest said earlier on Tuesday it would outsource non-core maintenance and service functions immediately, involving the retrenchment of 126 employees at Telfer and in support roles.</p>
<p>Newcrest has suffered from an unexpected loss of gold production this year from Telfer owing to heavier than normal rainfall at the mine site.  </p>
<p>The rains were forecast to reduce the mine's output by between 35,000 and 50,000 ounces in the 1996/97 year to June 30. The mine produced 365,000 ounces in 1995/96.</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
